# Trivy image-scan suppressions (.trivyignore format: CVE-ID per line, with
# optional justification as a comment ABOVE the entry — Trivy attaches the
# preceding comment block as the suppression reason in JSON/ASFF output).
#
# Gate policy: only suppress a CVE when its fixed version is recorded in the
# Alpine secdb (so `ignore-unfixed: true` doesn't already skip it) but the
# fixed package is NOT installable from the release repositories — verified
# against dl-cdn.alpinelinux.org, not a mirror. Every entry must carry a
# removal condition; re-run this check when the condition is met.

# CVE-2026-53612 CVE-2026-53613 CVE-2026-53614 CVE-2026-76642 CVE-2026-78408
# CVE-2026-78409 CVE-2026-78410 — util-linux / libuuid (alpine 3.24 main).
# Secdb records fixed version 2.42.3-r0, but as of 2026-09-05 that package is
# a 404 on dl-cdn.alpinelinux.org/alpine/v3.24/main/x86_64/ and APKINDEX only
# ships 2.42.1-r0, so `apk upgrade` (already run in the runtime stage) cannot
# pick it up. Exposure is minimal here: the runtime runs as the unprivileged
# `nyaya` user, does not invoke mount(8), and never runs nsenter.
# REMOVE WHEN: libuuid 2.42.3-r0 (or newer) appears in the v3.24 main repos —
# delete this entry and confirm the docker job goes green on its own.

CVE-2026-53612
CVE-2026-53613
CVE-2026-53614
CVE-2026-76642
CVE-2026-78408
CVE-2026-78409
